hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1115","Chapter on awarding the slayer the spoils of the slain, 1154 - al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: I heard Malik ibn Anas narrate, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Umar ibn Kathir ibn Aflah, from Abu Muhammad the freedman of Abu Qatadah, from Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Hunayn. When we met, the Muslims wavered at first. He said: I saw a man of the polytheists overpowering a Muslim man. He said: I circled round him until I came to him from behind and struck him on the cord of his shoulder. He turned on me and embraced me with an embrace in which I felt the scent of death. Then death overtook him and he released me. I caught up with Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: What is the matter with the people? He said: It is Allah's decree. He said: Then the people returned, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat and said: Whoever kills a slain man with proof thereof, his spoils are his. Abu Qatadah said: I stood and said: Who will bear witness for me? Then I sat down. Then he said again: Whoever kills a slain man with proof thereof, his spoils are his. He said: I stood and said: Who will bear witness for me? Then I sat down. Then he said it a third time, so I stood. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: What is the matter with you, O Abu Qatadah? He said: I told him the story. A man among the people said: He spoke the truth, O Messenger of Allah; the spoils of that slain man are with me, so compensate him for his due. Abu Bakr al-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) said: No, by Allah; he would not turn to a lion of Allah's lions fighting for Allah and His Messenger and then give you his spoils. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He spoke the truth; give them to him. So he gave them to me. He said: I sold the coat of mail and bought with its price a garden of date-palms among Banu Salamah; it was the first wealth I acquired in Islam. He said: And al-makhraf means date-palms."
"1116","1155 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr narrated to me, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashja'i and Khalid ibn al-Walid (may Allah be pleased with them), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not take a fifth from the spoils of the slain."
